169:- always writes `<D>/issue-summary.md` from `templates/issue-summary.md`: what the issue asks for, relevant files and systems (the cheatsheet), type, complexity, **effort estimate in hours** (B3) using the rubric in `refs/claim.md`, and links to anything under `<D>/analysis/`;
173:1. Invoke `Skill sc-recommend` with a goal built from `issue-summary.md`: issue URL, type, complexity, the summary path, and the default chain row for that type and complexity from `refs/chains.md` (section 9) as the suggested route. `/sc:recommend` picks the starting chain and depth (B4). Save its output verbatim to `<D>/recommend.md`.
174:2. Write `<D>/next-steps.md` from `templates/next-steps.md`: the `/model` line for the tier (B14, section 9), then the commands in order with their flags, the inputs each needs (`@.dev/issues/<N>/issue-summary.md`), the effort estimate, and, when `/sc:recommend` chose differently from the default row, one line naming the default row and why it was not used.
179:2. Claim comment: write `<D>/claim-comment.md` from `templates/claim-comment.md`: who claimed it, ClickUp result, the summary overview, effort estimate, complexity, and repo-relative links to `<D>/issue-summary.md`, `<D>/next-steps.md` and `<D>/analysis/` (default D9). It carries `<!-- sc:issue:claim -->`. Post or edit it the same way as step 1.
