261:Note (2026-11-04): the claim summary was renamed from `summary.md` to `issue-summary.md` (its template too, `templates/summary.md` to `templates/issue-summary.md`), and the `/sc:analyze` report under `analysis/` is now named `analyze-<scope>.md`. Cause: Claude Code's Write tool refuses any subagent write whose file basename matches `^(REPORT|SUMMARY|FINDINGS|ANALYSIS).*\.md$` (case-insensitive), with the error "Subagents should return findings as text, not write report files." This was found in live acceptance testing of #302, when issue-worker-t2's Write of `.dev/issues/365/summary.md` was refused, so claim Wave 4 could never produce its summary. No worker file name may start with analysis, report, summary or findings; `tests/skills/test_issue_worker_agents.py` now pins every file name a worker is told to write against that pattern and checks that no reference to the old summary path remains.
