439:| D22 | `issue-summary.md` is written on every claim; `/sc:analyze` runs only when the issue is out of date | The issue sizes and summarizes every claim; the analysis is the expensive part |
469:1. `/sc:issue --claim <N>` on an open, unassigned issue of the origin repo: the T3 worker runs first; the issue is assigned to the current user; `.dev/issues/<N>/` holds `scout.md`, `clickup.json`, `accuracy-check.md`, `issue-summary.md` (with an hours estimate), `recommend.md`, `next-steps.md`, `claim-comment.md`; two marked comments are posted; the command stops without running any next-step command.
